# switch-t210: ChromeOS delays udev-trigger by 30s via failsafe-delay's
# `exec sleep 30` to improve perceived boot time on devices where Chrome
# comes up fast (Chrome's `starting system-services` cancels the sleep
# early on normal boots).
#
# On Switch, Chrome's UI start is gated on nvgpu, and nvgpu probe is gated
# on udev-trigger (it's filtered out of udev-trigger-early's display/input
# subsystem allowlist).  Deadlock: UI fails for 30s waiting for nvgpu,
# upstart gives up, failsafe-delay finally fires → udev-trigger runs →
# nvgpu/brcmfmac/joycon/HCI all probe at once → UI works on next attempt.
#
# Break the cycle by firing udev-trigger on `started boot-services`
# instead.  boot-services is already up by T~8s, well before failsafe's
# 30s timeout would have triggered it.
start on started boot-services
